# Language policy

## After prompt81 Phase A (2026-07-21)

| Layer | Language | Examples |
|-------|----------|----------|
| **Language gate + Quick Start** | **`appLocale`** (`userLanguage`) | Wizard copy, units row labels, help `?` → `/{lang}/help/` |
| **Coach & meals & exports** | **`appLocale`** | Gemini chat, meal `name_local`, visit reports |
| **App UI chrome (Dashboard…)** | **English until Phase B** (`prompt81b`) | Screen titles, settings, Food Log chrome |
| **Clinic portal UI** | **English** | Clinician tool |
| **Website help** | **Path locale** | `https://healthings.ai/{en\|he\|es\|fr\|de\|ar\|ru}/help/…` |

## Always-English glossary

Brand, units (`kcal`, `mg/dL`, `kg`), acronyms (`CGM`, `BMR`), device names (Withings…), slash commands, product keys like `My Rules` / `My Profile` when used as proper names in mixed copy.

## Settings UX

One language preference drives coach, meals, Quick Start, and help links. Prefer **App & coach language** when renaming the Profile picker (Phase B).

## RTL

Hebrew/Arabic: RTL for Quick Start / user-content areas now; full chrome RTL with Phase B.

## Intent detection

Chat slash commands and natural-language triggers may stay multilingual (`chatIntent.ts`).

## When to revisit

Phase B (`prompt81b`) — Dashboard / Food Log / Profile label i18n. Until then keep remaining chrome English.
